OL,3,AUnder-fives and pregnant women told to
OL,4,Aavoid runny eggs when eating out over
OL,5,Asalmonella risk
OL,6,
OL,7,FVulnerable people are being warned not
OL,8,Fto eat under-cooked or runny eggs when
OL,9,Fthey are eating out because of the
OL,10,Fdeveloping salmonella outbreak.
OL,12,FThe Food Standards Agency (FSA) told
OL,13,Fthe BBC the under fives, over 65s,
OL,14,Fwomen who are pregnant and those with
OL,15,Fhealth conditions should avoid them
OL,16,Falong with freshly-made products that
OL,17,Fmight contain uncooked eggs, such as
OL,18,Fmayonnaise, souffle and hollandaise
OL,19,Fsauce.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
